==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Storm Beast Naala''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Naala''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP after completing [[Atonement for Sin]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Naala's unique way of attacking may seem hard to understand, so here's how it affects its performance:

*Enemies stalled <u>anywhere</u> in its range get hit <u>exactly once,</u> they thus take 1/3 of its full damage and DPS.
*Enemies approaching it have a chance to not be hit by the attack at all (faster = higher chance), as they may move from the range of an attack that is about to happen to the range of an attack that has just happened.
*Does NOT benefit from a higher de-buff chance/uptime that multi-hit attackers usually receive.
*Bases take damage from the closest hit that reaches them and all that overshoot, taking up to 100% of Naala's DPS (see [[Hitbox]] to understand why).
*Enemies hit while in specific positions, if knocked back, may very rarely be hit twice.

''Overall, it's like a normal attack with the chance to miss enemies and 1/3 the power outside of bases.''

While Naala technically has 15,031 DPS at level 30, in practice it will "only" be 5,010, which is still very good for a Long Distance attacker. The cost is its short standing range; most mid-ranged enemies can easily get the first hit on Naala, meaning that it has to rely on a stepping stone to safely snipe them. Worse still, it only has 1 standing range against enemy bases which means it can get easily ambushed by spawned enemies without having protection from meatshields. Nevertheless, its high health and immunities give it some usage in 4-Crown Uncanny Legends or in specific scenarios. In addition, standing so close to bases with few knockbacks has some potential for cheesing stages, as any non-boss enemy that spawns would not get in front of the base until Naala is half-dead, allowing DPS units that suffer from short range and/or Single Attack to safely whale on it for a short while.

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Naala gains several useful buffs that further improve its utility and survivability. At Lv.30, Naala's base HP increases from 71K to 85K, which is a ~19% increase. Its bulk allows it to absorb numerous attacks from targets before being knocked back, enabling Naala to serve as a quick source of generalist burst damage. However, even with these buffs, Naala is still unlikely to survive until the next one is available due to its limited range and sustainability.

The most important change here is the increase in its [[Weaken]] activation rate vs. Relics, going from 30% to 100%. Combined with [[Strong Against]], Naala reaches an effective 340K HP and 7.5K DPS at Lv.30 against Relics. This ludicrous effective HP, combined with its Long Distance Multi-Hits, and ~70% uptime on Weaken, means that Naala has the potential to control an entire battlefield. Additionally, Naala's Weaken ability synergizes exceptionally well with other [[Uncanny Legends]] units, most notably with [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]. Provided enemies are Weakened, Doguemon's already impressive health against Relics is boosted even further. This is especially apparent in stages like [[Revival of Origin]], where Naala's Weaken and Doguemon's high effective HP, accounting for Colossus Slayer, enables both of them to tank a massive amount of damage from [[Zero Luza]], crippling and stalling it until replacements are ready.

As with all many UL Mythic Units, Naala also gains the [[Behemoth Slayer|Behemoth]]/[[Colossus Slayer]] ability, boosting its DPS further by a magnification of 2.5x/1.6x respectively, enabling Naala to act as a dedicated counter to many [[Gauntlet|Colossus Gauntlets]] regardless of typing. Its specialist output against Behemoths surpasses that of its Relic targeting, at 12.5K DPS. However, its HP sits much lower at 142K, making it much more fragile considering its lack of Weaken, as well as Behemoth Slayer's defensive bonus being lower than Strong Against (0.6x > 0.5x). Against Relic Behemoths—specifically [[Ancient Magamojoe]] and [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]]—Naala's effective stats jump to 18.8K DPS and 283K HP at Lv.30. In the case of Ancient Magamojoe, Naala's Weaken increases its effective HP to a staggering 566K, and its immunity to Magamojoe's Surges makes it a perfect counter, regardless of the circumstances. While Naala is slightly less effective against Ibilujon due to the latter's higher damage and multiple immunities (notably Weaken), it still proves more than a match.

Awakened Naala is an incredibly valuable asset to your cat army, as well as one of the best anti-Relic units in the game. It is generally recommended to prioritize this True Form, as Epic Behemoth Stones are not easy to acquire.

