==Trivia==
*Elder Beast Naala and [[Ultima Beast Naala]] are the first characters to have multi-hit attacks with different effective ranges on each hit.
*The name Naala (ナーラ ''Nāra'') may be a reference to the Japanese city of [[wikipedia:Nara (city)|Nara]], which is famous for its deer. In fact, Naala and Nara sound almost the same in Japanese.
*Elder Beast Naala's Japanese description refers to it as a ''[[wikipedia:Raijū|raijū]]'' (雷獣, "thunder-beast"), a Japanese legendary creature that has a body made of lightning and is represented with the form of many different animals, including a deer or [[wikipedia:Qilin|qilin/kirin]] - a holy, unicorn-like beast from Chinese mythology that is often depicted with deer-like traits, particularly in Japan.
**Naala may specifically be based on [[wikia:monsterhunter:Kirin|Kirin]] from ''Monster Hunter'', as its ability to rapidly call down series of lightning bolts is very similar to ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s Kirin's attacks and its enemy form is a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], which tend to be references to ''Monster Hunter''.
**Naala's Normal/Evolved Form's color scheme also gives it some resemblance to the Pokémon [[bulbapedia:Arceus (Pokémon)|Arceus]].
*Elder Beast Naala may represent [[wikipedia:Eikþyrnir|Eikþyrnir]], a heavenly stag in Norse mythology. Awakened Naala is stated to be holy, and Eikþyrnir eats from [[wikipedia:Læraðr|Læraðr]], a tree often identified with [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]]—a possible inspiration for the [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in the last four [[Uncanny Legends]] stages. The dew that drips from Eikþyrnir's glowing antlers flows into [[wikipedia:Hvergelmir|Hvergelmir]], one of the wellsprings at Yggdrasil's roots, creating rivers that sustain life; this may be referenced by the stage before [[Immortal Zenith]], [[Silver Current]], whose Japanese name confirms that it refers to a water current. Eikþyrnir stands upon one of the afterlife locations, [[wikipedia:Valhalla|Valhalla]], which may correlate or contrast with [[Immortal Zenith]], whose Japanese name (天寿を授ける頂 ''Tenju o Sazukeru Itadaki'') can be literally translated as "The Summit That Bestows Natural Lifespans".
*Unlike other [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]], Elder Beast Naala's preview displayed when entering [[Legend Stages]] shows its enemy counterpart: one can tell from the shape of its tail and the idol on its back.

